{"team":"IND","col":"#4F9BE8","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":60.1,"adot":9.3,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Balanced Attack</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Jonathan Taylor</strong> absorbs <strong>80% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>20%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (80% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p>They push it downfield \u2014 average depth of target <strong>9.3 yards</strong> with 24% of throws traveling 15+, a vertical passing game that trades completions for boom-or-bust yardage.</p><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (20% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (44% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Jonathan Taylor</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 No Obvious Seam</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 68 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing tight ends</strong> \u2014 42 rec yds/game (vs ~35). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>118 rushing</strong> and <strong>253 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: no single dominant angle \u2014 this one's a matchup-by-matchup read.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Daniel Jones","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":15,"props":{"Comp":7.06,"At